>to search on a given spot 100 times.  If a nasty showed up, or you got
>hungry, or anything really happened, it would stop.  This was VERY
>useful....  I'm tired of dying because the autorepeat on my "s" key got
>away from me.
>

On some machines (like mine) the numeric keypad is no different than 
the numbers on the top of the keyboard.  Hence, if you turn the 
number_pad option on, "147s" would mean (go sw)(go w)(go nw)(search),
not search 147 times (or until something interesting happens).  The
standard way of doing that one any (?) machine is "n147s".


